If the high price tag of premium 3D printers have kept you from exploring the hobby, this deal is a great entry point. Elegoo has its on sale for $369, almost $100 off its usual price of $449. This capable 3D printer can handle four filament rolls at once, with a fully enclosed printing area, auto-leveling bed, and big touchscreen for easy project management. It’saltogether very capable 3D printer for beginners, or just anyone who doesn’t want to spend a lot of time tinkering with settings just to print occasional trinkets and brackets.The Centauri Carbon 2 is fast and capable right out of the box, though first-time setup is a little involved (I found it tough to get the upper shield and filament hub to fit together, for example). But I really like its fully-enclosed build area, which results in consistent prints, and the auto-leveling bed checks that everything is locked in the right place before each print. It’s worth noting that the filament rolls are stored externally, so if you’re in a particularly humid environment and don’t print often, you may want to remove them between uses.
window.HYPE_DESK_CONFIG = { productImageUrl: "https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/ChatGPT-Image-Sep-3-2026-10_19_50-AM.png", productImageAlt: "HOTO Pulse 4-in-1 Cordless Stapler", productTitle: "HOTO Pulse 4-in-1 Cordless Stapler", shortDescription: "The stapler that tells you what it is doing.", longDescription: "Most staplers give you no information until the moment they fail. The HOTO Pulse tracks your remaining staples in real time, confirms when it is ready to fire, and handles four staple and nail types so one tool covers more of your projects. A built-in remover means quick fixes happen on the spot. Compact, lightweight, and genuinely useful.", purchaseUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H74SXNTQ?&linkCode=ll2&tag=theverge02-20&linkId=186f55593bda58be43b5d716980c0045&language=en_US&gaOptInStatus=true&ref_=as_li_ss_tl", purchaseLinkText: "Shop At Amazon" };
The in purple is on sale for $15 off at B&H Photo for a limited time, bringing the price down to just $35 when the $5 coupon is applied in your cart. This very portable Bluetooth speaker is IP67-rated for water and dust resistance, with up to seven hours of playback on a single charge, and USB-C charging.Nintendo has temporarily dropped the price on a variety of accessories as part of its “Customer Appreciation” sale, including the . Amazon has the neon purple and orange pair on sale for $62.97, almost $30 lower than the list price. These work wirelessly with the Switch 2 as well, although you’ll need a dedicated charging dock.If you’re running out of ports and plugs nearby, Anker’s Prime Charging Station is a great purchase to consider while it’s $59.99 (usually $79.99) at Amazon. This 6-in-1 travel-ready charging station has two AC outlets, two USB-A ports, and two USB-C ports (either tops out at 140W when it’s the only port in use). The included power cable is five feet long, and detaches from the unit for easier storage.
